  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 127 PM CDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nCurrent surface analysis places low over the Great Basin nudging\ntowards the northern Rockies, while high is situated over the \nsouthern Prairie Provinces into the upper Midwest. Upper level \nanalysis places low off the Pacific Northwest, with ridge over \nthe central/northern plains. Over our area, light easterly flow \nis keeping some low clouds/fog anchored over parts of southwest \nNorth Dakota. The fog has remained dense over far southwest \nNorth Dakota where a Dense Fog Advisory remains in places \nthrough 1PM MDT, but some improvement in visibility has been \nnoted on area webcams and observations so plan to let it expire \nat that time.\n\nFor the rest of today into tonight, low level southeast flow\nremains in place, with clouds and some fog returning from\nsouthwest to northeast overnight. A variety of weak waves\nlifting ahead of aforementioned upper trough may bring a few \nweak light showers to the area, in addition to some possible \ndrizzle given the light upslope moist low level flow.\n\nAs we get into tomorrow, light upslope flow continues with\nclouds lingering over the area. Main concern with this is its\ninfluence on temperatures as think latest NBM is much too\noptimistic with its high temperature forecast. Therefore, have \nleaned towards NBM10 which still may be too optimistic over the\nsouth central/southwest, but at least it starts the downward\ntrend. Have also kept the potential for fog in the forecast\nthrough mid-day. Given the light southeasterly low level flow\ncontinuing into Saturday night and Sunday morning, have \nreturned the fog throughout the area.\n\nPrecipitation chances will be on a significant increase Sunday\nnight into Monday as the aforementioned upper low works its way\nover the Rockies, and a surface low spins up to the lee of the\nCentral Rockies and ejects into the central plains. This looks\nto bring widespread precipitation to the area, though \ntemperature profiles remain warm enough so this should remain \nliquid. A few rumbles of thunder from an elevated thunderstorms \ncan not be ruled out over southern portions of the area. \n\nThereafter some questions remain with the forecast as guidance\nhas been leaning towards ridging, but some ensemble members lean\ntowards a bit more active pattern. With that said, temperatures\nlook to remain seasonal.",
